From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prokrypt <prokrypt@edited.us>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] pinebook-pro: SPL boot order SPI flash, eMMC, SD card

Patch 0039 made SPL load the U-Boot FIT from the SD card first. With
Rockchip's DDR blob as TPL and Rockchip's BL31 in the SPI FIT, that is a
trap: any card with a U-Boot FIT at sector 0x4000 (Manjaro ARM, Armbian,
Tow-Boot installer cards) inserted at power-on is booted instead, its
upstream TF-A leaves the DMACs secure-only and the first DRAM rate change
hangs the machine.

Try the SPI flash first, then the eMMC, then the SD card. This is the
order the SPL in daily use since 2026-10-29 had binary-patched into its
device tree; this patch makes the source match it.
---
 arch/arm/dts/rk3399-pinebook-pro-u-boot.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-pinebook-pro-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-pinebook-pro-u-boot.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-pinebook-pro-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-pinebook-pro-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 
 / {
 	chosen {
-		u-boot,spl-boot-order = &sdmmc, &spiflash, &sdhci;
+		u-boot,spl-boot-order = &spiflash, &sdhci, &sdmmc;
 	};
 
 	config {
